**1. A starter-generator system comprising:**  

a dynamoelectric machine including a stator, a rotor having a plurality of permanent magnets providing rotor excitation, and first and second electrically separate multiphase stator windings forming parallel electrical channels and magnetically coupled to the rotor;  

a first power converter electrically coupled to the first multiphase stator winding;  

a second power converter electrically coupled to the second multiphase stator winding; and  

a controller coupled to the first and second power converters and configured to:  

operate at least the first power converter in a starting mode to supply multiphase current to the first multiphase stator winding and thereby produce torque for rotating the rotor;  

receive signals representative of multiphase output voltages of the second multiphase stator winding;  

determine, without a rotor-position sensor, an estimated angular position of the rotor based at least in part on the multiphase output voltages of the second multiphase stator winding;  

control commutation of at least the first power converter based on the estimated angular position; and  

operate the first and second power converters in a generating mode to convert electrical power generated in the respective first and second multiphase stator windings into power supplied to a direct-current electrical bus.
